-- coa19-a1-after.l4: Part 25, Chapter A1, cross-headings "Consequence of non-delivery" and "The register":
-- ss 859H to 859O, lines 11700-11814 of ukpga-2006-46.txt. Layer 1: the law as the text states it.
--
-- SEAMS taken as inputs (PLAN.md section 4): `s 1062 the document bears the registrar's official seal` (coa23, MAYBE BOOLEAN) in s 859I(5);
-- `s 1170A the person is a receiver or manager` is NOT asked: the facts of s 859K(1) are stated as the text states them.
-- Judgments the text hands to the court ("if the court is satisfied") are plain inputs.
-- Answers are MAYBE BOOLEAN unless a DATE or a table; see coa19-nouns.l4 for how to read them.

§ `Part 25 Company charges -- Chapter A1 -- Consequence of non-delivery, the register (ss 859H to 859O)`

§§ `s 859H Consequence of failure to deliver charges`

-- (2): the relevant period is the period under the section in question, or the period the court's order allows
-- src:11705 | (2) “The relevant period allowed for delivery” is—
-- src:11706 | (a) the period allowed for delivery under the section in question, or
-- src:11707 | (b) if an order under section 859F(3) has been made, the period allowed by the order.
@ref s 859H(2) The relevant period allowed for delivery (src:11705-11707)
GIVEN `the last day of the period allowed for delivery under the section in question` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period allowed by an order under section 859F(3)` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 859H(2) the last day of the relevant period allowed for delivery` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the last day of the period allowed by an order under section 859F(3)`
    WHEN JUST lastDay THEN lastDay
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the last day of the period allowed for delivery under the section in question`

-- src:11702 | (1) This section applies if—
-- src:11703 | (a) a company creates a charge to which section 859A or 859B applies, and
-- src:11704 | (b) the documents required by section 859A or (as the case may be) 859B are not delivered to the registrar by the company or another person interested in the charge before the end of the relevant period allowed for delivery.
@ref s 859H(1) This section applies if (src:11702-11704)
GIVEN `section 859A applies to the charge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 859B applies to the charge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the documents required by section 859A or 859B were delivered to the registrar by the company or another person interested in the charge before the end of the relevant period` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 859H(1) this section applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `section 859A applies to the charge`) AND (NOT `section 859B applies to the charge`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a company creates a charge to which section 859A or 859B applies"
        IF `the documents required by section 859A or 859B were delivered to the registrar by the company or another person interested in the charge before the end of the relevant period` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies if—"
        IF `the documents required by section 859A or 859B were delivered to the registrar by the company or another person interested in the charge before the end of the relevant period` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): it is not yet known whether the documents were delivered in time

DECLARE `s 859H(3) party against whom the charge may be void` IS ONE OF
    `s 859H(3)(a) a liquidator of the company`
    `s 859H(3)(b) an administrator of the company`
    `s 859H(3)(c) a creditor of the company`
    `s 859H(3) any other person`

-- src:11708 | (3) Where this section applies, the charge is void (so far as any security on the company's property or undertaking is conferred by it) against—
-- src:11709 | (a) a liquidator of the company,
-- src:11710 | (b) an administrator of the company, and
-- src:11711 | (c) a creditor of the company.
@ref s 859H(3) the charge is void (so far as any security on the company's property or undertaking is conferred by it) against (src:11708-11711)
GIVEN `s 859H(1) this section applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      party IS A `s 859H(3) party against whom the charge may be void`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 859H(3) the charge is void against the party` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 859H(1) this section applies`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where this section applies, the charge is void"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent)
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        CONSIDER party
        WHEN `s 859H(3) any other person` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "the charge is void (so far as any security on the company's property or undertaking is conferred by it) against—": the list names three kinds of person and is not closed with "only"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:11712 | (4) Subsection (3) is without prejudice to any contract or obligation for repayment of the money secured by the charge; and when a charge becomes void under this section, the money secured by it immediately becomes payable.
@ref s 859H(4) Subsection (3) is without prejudice to any contract or obligation for repayment of the money secured by the charge (src:11712-11712)
GIVEN `there is a contract or obligation for repayment of the money secured by the charge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 859H(4) subsection (3) prejudices the contract or obligation for repayment of the money secured by the charge` MEANS
    IF `there is a contract or obligation for repayment of the money secured by the charge`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (3) is without prejudice to any contract or obligation for repayment of the money secured by the charge"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): there is nothing for subsection (3) to prejudice

-- src:11712 | (4) Subsection (3) is without prejudice to any contract or obligation for repayment of the money secured by the charge; and when a charge becomes void under this section, the money secured by it immediately becomes payable.
@ref s 859H(4) when a charge becomes void under this section, the money secured by it immediately becomes payable (src:11712-11712)
GIVEN `s 859H(3) the charge is void against the party` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 859H(4) the money secured by the charge immediately becomes payable` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 859H(3) the charge is void against the party`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "when a charge becomes void under this section, the money secured by it immediately becomes payable": "when" counts as "where"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent)

§§ `s 859I Entries on the register`

