        CONSIDER document
        WHEN `s 859I(2)(b) any other document` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "include in the register any documents delivered under section 859A(3) or (5), 859B(3), (4) or (7), or 859C(3)": the list names the documents; the text says nothing of any other
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:11719 | (3) The registrar must give a certificate of the registration of the charge to the person who delivered to the registrar a section 859D statement of particulars relating to the charge.
@ref s 859I(3) The registrar must give a certificate of the registration of the charge to the person who delivered the statement (src:11719-11719)
GIVEN `s 859I(1) this section applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person delivered to the registrar a section 859D statement of particulars relating to the charge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 859I(3) the registrar must give the person a certificate of the registration of the charge` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 859I(1) this section applies`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where a charge is registered"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent)
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the person delivered to the registrar a section 859D statement of particulars relating to the charge`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to the person who delivered to the registrar a section 859D statement of particulars relating to the charge"

DECLARE `s 859I(4) what the certificate states` IS ONE OF
