         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The certificate must be signed by the registrar or authenticated by the registrar's official seal"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the certificate bears the official seal is s 1062, which another part answers

-- src:11724 | (6) In the case of registration under section 859A or 859B, the certificate is conclusive evidence that the documents required by the section concerned were delivered to the registrar before the end of the relevant period allowed for delivery.
