      `the person is the company or a person interested in the charge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 859J(1) the person may deliver to the registrar a statement that the company is acting as trustee` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the company is acting as trustee of property or undertaking which is the subject of a charge delivered for registration under Chapter A1`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a company is acting as trustee of property or undertaking which is the subject of a charge delivered for registration under this Chapter"
        IF `the person is the company or a person interested in the charge` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the company or any person interested in the charge may deliver"

