-- src:11745 | (i) in the case of a charge created before 6th April 2013, the information specified in subsection (4), or
-- src:11746 | (ii) in the case of a charge created on or after 6th April 2013, the unique reference code allocated to the charge.
@ref s 859K(3)(b) give the registrar a notice containing (src:11744-11746)
GIVEN `the date of creation of the charge` IS A DATE
      item IS A `s 859K(4) item of information`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 859K(3)(b) the notice to the registrar must contain the item` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF item EQUALS `s 859K anything else` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "give the registrar a notice containing—"
        IF `the date of creation of the charge` LESS THAN Date 6 4 2013 AND item EQUALS `s 859K(2)(b)(ii) the unique reference code allocated to the charge`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the case of a charge created on or after 6th April 2013, the unique reference code allocated to the charge": this charge was created before 6 April 2013
        IF `the date of creation of the charge` LESS THAN Date 6 4 2013
        THEN JUST TRUE -- the text requires, "in the case of a charge created before 6th April 2013, the information specified in subsection (4)": items (a) to (c) of subsection (4)
        IF item EQUALS `s 859K(2)(b)(ii) the unique reference code allocated to the charge` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the case of a charge created before 6th April 2013, the information specified in subsection (4)": this charge was created on or after 6 April 2013, so the subsection (4) information is not required

DECLARE `s 859K(5) fact of which notice is given` IS ONE OF
    `s 859K(5)(a) a fact of which notice is given under subsection (2)(a)`
    `s 859K(5)(b) a fact of which notice is given under subsection (3)(a)`
    `s 859K(5) any other fact`

-- src:11751 | (5) The registrar must include in the register—
-- src:11752 | (a) a fact of which notice is given under subsection (2)(a), and
-- src:11753 | (b) a fact of which notice is given under subsection (3)(a).
@ref s 859K(5) The registrar must include in the register (src:11751-11753)
GIVEN fact IS A `s 859K(5) fact of which notice is given`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 859K(5) the registrar must include the fact in the register` MEANS
    CONSIDER fact
    WHEN `s 859K(5) any other fact` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "The registrar must include in the register—"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:11754 | (6) A person who makes default in complying with the requirements of subsections (2) or (3) of this section commits an offence.
@ref s 859K(6) A person who makes default in complying with the requirements of subsections (2) or (3) of this section commits an offence (src:11754-11754)
GIVEN `s 859K(1), (8) and (9) the person must give notice to the registrar` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person made default in complying with the requirements of subsection (2) or (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 859K(6) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 859K(1), (8) and (9) the person must give notice to the registrar` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person who makes default in complying with the requirements of subsections (2) or (3) of this section commits an offence": no requirement of subsection (2) or (3) binds the person
        IF `s 859K(1), (8) and (9) the person must give notice to the registrar` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent)
        IF `the person made default in complying with the requirements of subsection (2) or (3)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person who makes default in complying with the requirements of subsections (2) or (3) of this section commits an offence": no default

-- src:11755 | (7) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 859K(7) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale (src:11755-11755)
`s 859K(7) the penalty for the offence` MEANS
    Penalty OF `on summary conviction`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1), JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1), FALSE

§§ `s 859L Entries of satisfaction and release`

-- src:11762 | (2) The statement referred to in subsection (1) is a statement to the effect that—
-- src:11763 | (a) the debt for which the charge was given has been paid or satisfied in whole or in part, or
-- src:11764 | (b) all or part of the property or undertaking charged—
-- src:11765 | (i) has been released from the charge, or
-- src:11766 | (ii) has ceased to form part of the company's property or undertaking.
@ref s 859L(2) The statement referred to in subsection (1) is a statement to the effect that (src:11762-11766)
GIVEN `the statement says that the debt for which the charge was given has been paid or satisfied in whole or in part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement says that all or part of the property or undertaking charged has been released from the charge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement says that all or part of the property or undertaking charged has ceased to form part of the company's property or undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 859L(2) the statement is the statement the section describes` MEANS
    IF       `the statement says that the debt for which the charge was given has been paid or satisfied in whole or in part`
         OR  `the statement says that all or part of the property or undertaking charged has been released from the charge`
         OR  `the statement says that all or part of the property or undertaking charged has ceased to form part of the company's property or undertaking`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The statement referred to in subsection (1) is a statement to the effect that—"

-- src:11767 | (3) Where a statement within subsection (2)(b) relates to part only of the property or undertaking charged, the statement must include a short description of that part.
@ref s 859L(3) Where a statement within subsection (2)(b) relates to part only of the property or undertaking charged, the statement must include a short description of that part (src:11767-11767)
GIVEN `the statement is within subsection (2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement relates to part only of the property or undertaking charged` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 859L(3) the statement must include a short description of that part` MEANS
    IF `the statement is within subsection (2)(b)` AND `the statement relates to part only of the property or undertaking charged`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a statement within subsection (2)(b) relates to part only of the property or undertaking charged"

-- src:11768 | (4) The particulars referred to in subsection (1) are—
-- src:11769 | (a) the name and address of the person delivering the statement and an indication of their interest in the charge;
-- src:11770 | (b) the registered name and number of the company that—
-- src:11771 | (i) created the charge (in a case within section 859A or 859B), or
-- src:11772 | (ii) acquired the property or undertaking subject to the charge (in a case within section 859C);
-- src:11773 | (c) in respect of a charge created before 6th April 2013—
-- src:11774 | (i) the date of creation of the charge;
-- src:11775 | (ii) a description of the instrument (if any) by which the charge is created or evidenced;
-- src:11776 | (iii) short particulars of the property or undertaking charged;
-- src:11777 | (d) in respect of a charge created on or after 6th April 2013, the unique reference code allocated to the charge.
@ref s 859L(4) The particulars referred to in subsection (1) are (src:11768-11777)
GIVEN `the particulars give the name and address of the person delivering the statement and an indication of their interest in the charge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the particulars give the registered name and number of the company that created the charge or acquired the property or undertaking subject to it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of creation of the charge` IS A DATE
      `the charge is created or evidenced by an instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the particulars give the date of creation of the charge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the particulars give a description of the instrument by which the charge is created or evidenced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the particulars give short particulars of the property or undertaking charged` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the particulars give the unique reference code allocated to the charge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 859L(4) the particulars set out in subsection (4) are delivered` MEANS
    IF       `the particulars give the name and address of the person delivering the statement and an indication of their interest in the charge`
         AND `the particulars give the registered name and number of the company that created the charge or acquired the property or undertaking subject to it`
         AND (    (    `the date of creation of the charge` LESS THAN Date 6 4 2013
                   AND `the particulars give the date of creation of the charge`
                   AND ((NOT `the charge is created or evidenced by an instrument`) OR `the particulars give a description of the instrument by which the charge is created or evidenced`)
                   AND `the particulars give short particulars of the property or undertaking charged`)
              OR  (    `the date of creation of the charge` AT LEAST Date 6 4 2013
                   AND `the particulars give the unique reference code allocated to the charge`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The particulars referred to in subsection (1) are—"

-- src:11761 | (1) Subsection (5) applies if the statement set out in subsection (2) and the particulars set out in subsection (4) are delivered to the registrar with respect to a registered charge.
@ref s 859L(1) Subsection (5) applies if the statement set out in subsection (2) and the particulars set out in subsection (4) are delivered to the registrar (src:11761-11761)
GIVEN `s 859L(2) the statement is the statement the section describes` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 859L(4) the particulars set out in subsection (4) are delivered` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the statement and the particulars are delivered to the registrar with respect to a registered charge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 859L(1) subsection (5) applies` MEANS
    IF       (`s 859L(2) the statement is the statement the section describes` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
         AND (`s 859L(4) the particulars set out in subsection (4) are delivered` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
         AND `the statement and the particulars are delivered to the registrar with respect to a registered charge`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (5) applies if the statement set out in subsection (2) and the particulars set out in subsection (4) are delivered to the registrar with respect to a registered charge"

DECLARE `s 859L(5) what the registrar includes` IS ONE OF
    `s 859L(5)(a) a statement of satisfaction in whole or in part`
    `s 859L(5)(b) a statement of the fact that all or part of the property or undertaking has been released from the charge or has ceased to form part of the company's property or undertaking`
    `s 859L(5) anything else`

